[00:13.06] I recall when I was small
[00:15.40] How I spent my days alone
[00:18.87] The busy world was not for me
[00:21.48] So I went and found my own
[00:25.31] I would climb the garden wall
[00:27.57] With a candle in my hand
[00:30.50] I'd hide inside a hall of rock and sand
[00:37.35] On the stone an ancient hand
[00:39.84] In a faded yellow-green
[00:43.55] Made alive a worldly wonder
[00:46.07] Often told but never seen
[00:49.77] Now and ever bound to labor
[00:52.24] On the sea and in the sky
[00:55.67] Every man and beast appeared
[00:58.47] A friend as real as I
[01:01.28] Before the fall when they wrote it on the wall
[01:04.54] When there wasn't even any Hollywood
[01:07.24] They heard the call and they wrote it on the wall
[01:10.78] For you and me, we understood
[01:13.90] 
